### Variables
@host = http://localhost:3000
@authToken = your-secret-auth-key

### 1. Healthcheck (Public)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/healthz
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Get Sync Stats (Authenticated)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/sync/stats
X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Get Sync History (Authenticated)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/sync-history?page=1&size=15
X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Post Customer Sync - Insert (Authenticated)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sync
X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "customers",
  "data": [
    {
      "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
      "first_name": "Jane",
      "last_name": "Doe",
      "default_currency": "USD"
    }
  ]
}

###

### 5. Post Customer Sync - Upsert/Update (Authenticated)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sync
X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "customers",
  "data": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
      "first_name": "Jane",
      "last_name": "Smith",
      "default_currency": "EUR"
    }
  ]
}

###

### 6. Post Product Sync (Authenticated)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sync
X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "products",
  "data": [
    {
      "name": "Wireless Mouse",
      "description": "Ergonomic 2.4GHz wireless mouse",
      "price": 2500,
      "currency": "USD",
      "active": true,
      "weight_grams": 150
    }
  ]
}

###

### 7. Post Order Sync (Authenticated)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sync
X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "orders",
  "data": [
    {
      "order_number": "ORD-2026-0001",
      "customer_id": 1,
      "status": "pending",
      "currency": "USD",
      "amount": 5000,
      "items": [
        {
          "product_id": 1,
          "qty": 2,
          "unit_price": 2500
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

###

### 8. Post Employee Sync (Authenticated)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sync
X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "employees",
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "101",
      "employeeId": "EMP101",
      "firstName": "John",
      "lastName": "Doe",
      "email": "john.doe@example.com",
      "company": "Sync Bridge Corp",
      "jobTitle": "Software Engineer",
      "department": "Engineering"
    }
  ]
}

###

### 9. GraphQL Query - Search Employees (Public Query)
POST {{host}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { search_employees(search: \"\", limit: 5) { id employeeId firstName lastName email full_name } }"
}

###

### 10. GraphQL Mutation - Create Employee (Authenticated Mutation)
POST {{host}}/graphql
X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation { create_employee(data: { id: 100, employeeId: \"EMP100\", firstName: \"John\", lastName: \"Doe\", email: \"john.doe@example.com\" }) { id employeeId firstName lastName full_name } }"
}
